1
00:00:00,993 --> 00:00:03,033
- That is correct.
- I knew that too.

2
00:00:03,912 --> 00:00:06,582
(Penny:)Good for you, sweetie.
Okay, next question.

3
00:00:06,748 --> 00:00:10,458
"What is the quantum-mechanical effect
used to encode data on hard-disk drives?"

4
00:00:10,627 --> 00:00:11,667
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

5
00:00:11,837 --> 00:00:15,087
- Howard?
- The answer is giant magnetoresistance.

6
00:00:15,257 --> 00:00:17,337
(Leslie:)- Right.
- Hey, I buzzed in.

7
00:00:17,509 --> 00:00:20,049
And I answered. It's called teamwork.

8
00:00:21,722 --> 00:00:25,312
(Howard:)Don't you think I should answer
engineering questions? I am an engineer.

9
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:30,317
By that logic, I should answer anthropology
questions because I'm a mammal.

10
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:34,109
(Leonard:)Just ask another one.

11
00:00:34,276 --> 00:00:35,406
(Raj:)Okay.

12
00:00:35,569 --> 00:00:39,909
"What artificial satellite has seen glimpses
of Einstein's predicted 'frame dragging'?"

13
00:00:40,073 --> 00:00:41,113
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

14
00:00:41,283 --> 00:00:43,413
(Sheldon:)And, of course, it's Gravity Probe B.

15
00:00:43,577 --> 00:00:46,327
(Leonard:)Sheldon, you have to let
somebody else answer.

16
00:00:46,496 --> 00:00:48,786
(Howard:)- Why?
- Because it's polite.

17
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:52,756
(Sheldon:)What do manners have to do with it?
This is war.

18
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,840
(Sheldon:)Were the Romans polite
when they salted Carthage...

19
00:00:56,006 --> 00:00:58,466
(Sheldon:)...to make sure
nothing would ever grow again?

20
00:00:59,092 --> 00:01:04,022
(Penny:)Leonard, you said
I only had to ask questions.

